```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "recommendation",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_k8s_deployment_name, metric, min(value) AS vmin, max(value) AS vmax, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name = 'recommendation' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Recommendation deployment reports available=0 for every sample across the whole abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name = 'recommendation-69bf88479c-jwhg7' AND metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Recommendation pod restart counter climbs from 2 to 6 during the abnormal window, showing crash-looping; it was 1 in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT count(*) AS abnormal_recommendation_spans FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'recommendation'", "claim": "Recommendation emits zero spans in the abnormal window, versus 115 in the normal window."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "recommendation", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [
       {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'HTTP /recommendations' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "All 171 user-facing frontend HTTP /recommendations requests return 500 in the abnormal window; none in normal."},
       {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT count(*) AS n, min(time) AS first_seen FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND level = 'ERROR' AND message = 'Recommendation service failed'", "claim": "Frontend logs 56 ERROR entries stating 'Recommendation service failed' during the abnormal window."}
     ]}
  ]
}
```

The degradation comes from one fault: the recommendation service lost its pod. Its only instance is crash-looping, so the deployment reports zero available replicas for the whole abnormal window. The fault is classed as `pod_unavailable`, which is in the same equivalence class as `pod_failure`.

Recommendation stops producing spans entirely (115 in normal, 0 in abnormal). Frontend's `/recommendations` route returns HTTP 500 on all 171 of its requests, starting at 03:16:11, and frontend logs 56 "Recommendation service failed" errors. That is the only user-visible failure, and the frontend error share of 0.20 in the survey comes from it.

The other shifts in the survey (lower span counts in reservation, search, rate and profile, and changes in memcached timings) show no new errors, restarts or pod changes, so I attributed them to the changed request mix rather than to separate faults.

